   "title": "Two months under siege",
   "time": "14 July – 11 September",
   "narrative": "Since 14 July the Ottoman army of Grand Vizier Kara Mustafa has sat before Vienna, where Count Starhemberg commands a garrison and militia. Ottoman sappers have dug toward the north-western bastions and laid ten mines under them; the Ottoman camp lies south-west of the city, and janissaries hold the fortified post at the Türkenschanze and the villages Nussdorf and Heiligenstadt to the north. The city is close to falling.",
