   "time": "11 September evening",
   "narrative": "The relief army arrives over the Vienna Woods after crossing the Danube upstream. Poles under King John III Sobieski, Imperial troops under Charles of Lorraine, and Saxon, Bavarian and other German contingents gather on the Kahlenberg slopes and light bonfires to tell the city help is near. Jerzy Kulczycki, a Polish-born Turkish speaker, had slipped through the Ottoman lines with word of the plan. The Crimean Tatars under the khan, charged with guarding the rear, had refused to contest the crossing.",
